### Remarks  
 This method is used to perform a control-based unit test on the \`Insert\(\)\` method of the \`ArrayList\` class. The test includes input values, precondition, method execution, method postconditions and output values. The test harness is built using Pex's Assumes.  
  
### Example  
 The following is a unit test method for the \`AddRange\(\)\` method of the \`ArrayList\` class.  
  
```  
  
using System.Collections;  
using System.Diagnostics;  
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework;  
using NUnit.Framework;  
  
namespace ArrayList.Test  
{  
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest  
    {  
        [PexMethod]  
        public void AddRangeContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, ArrayList data)  
        {  
            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;  
            int Old_dataCount = data.Count;  
  
            arrList.AddRange(data);  
  
            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;  
  
            // Assertion of pre and post conditions  
  
            // Precondition: Count of data should be more than or equal to 0  
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_data_Count", Old_dataCount);  
  
            // Post condition: Count of arrayList should be added with the Count of data  
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);  
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_Count", New_arrListCount);  
  
            Assert.IsTrue(Old_dataCount >= 0);  
            Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + Old_dataCount);  
        }  
    }  
}  
  
```  
  
 The following is a unit test method for the Clear\(\) method.  
  
```  
  
using System;  
using System.Diagnostics;  
using System.Collections;  
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework;  
using NUnit.Framework;  
  
namespace ArrayList.Test {
  
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest {
  
        public void ClearContract([PexAssumeUnderTest] ArrayList arrList) {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(arrList.Count > 0);
  
            arrList.Clear();
	    // Assertion
            Assert.IsTrue(arrList.Count == 0);
        }
    }
}
```  
  
### Remarks  
 This is a contract test for the Clear method of the ArrayList class. The test includes an assumption under the testing class ArrayList (which is under test), it then triggers the method, and concludes the test by performing an assertion on the post condition method execution. If the post-condition is not met, the assertion will throw an exception and indicate that the method under test has failed. This indicates that the method Clear was not implemented correctly. It is a contract that is used for unit testing of the ArrayList class to check if everything works as expected.  
  
### Example  
